{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question","id":911346,"title":"Obfuscate Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-09T18:49:45-07:00","id":911346,"title":"Obfuscate Question","content":"When under the affects of Obfuscate. Is there anyway for anyone other then Mekhet to see through it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T18:58:40-07:00","id":911356,"title":"","content":"Yes. A high perception rating can work. Get merits to boost your perception checks and/or kindred senses. Get merits to boost your resistance or grants immunity to mind control powers or illusions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:11:31-07:00","id":911368,"title":"","content":"Lashing out also breaks Obfuscate 3 for sure, likely the others as well. But as Tsusasi said, Perception check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T19:35:55-07:00","id":911383,"title":"","content":"And you don't need to be Mekhet to learn Auspex. You just need a few drops of a Mekhet's blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T20:03:54-07:00","id":911402,"title":"","content":"Not sure how perception is going to work unless you suspect a kindred using obfuscate is there already, and there are context clues to queue off of (Which may not be the case in most circumstances unless you've set up some sort of situation for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:08:04-07:00","id":911431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911402#post911402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how perception is going to work unless you suspect a kindred using obfuscate is there already, and there are context clues to queue off of (Which may not be the case in most circumstances unless you've set up some sort of situation for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats what I'm wondering, like is it reflexive or does the person need a reason to suspect?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T21:09:01-07:00","id":911432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911356#post911356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. A high perception rating can work. Get merits to boost your perception checks and/or kindred senses. Get merits to boost your resistance or grants immunity to mind control powers or illusions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When would the person be allowed to roll to notice? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911368#post911368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lashing out also breaks Obfuscate 3 for sure, likely the others as well. But as Tsusasi said, Perception check.</div> </div> </div> </div>How can they lash if they don't know where the kindred is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:02:41-07:00","id":911452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911402#post911402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure how perception is going to work unless you suspect a kindred using obfuscate is there already, and there are context clues to queue off of (Which may not be the case in most circumstances unless you've set up some sort of situation for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate users don't go inert and cease interacting with their surroundings after activating their power, they immediately move to take full situational advantage or attempt to flee if they know they're likely to lose in a physical altercation. Someone with a high perception rating and/or appropriate skills (Investigation Specialty obfuscate use) and merits (Trained Observer, Unseen Sense, Danger Sense) are either already going to sense or know something's amiss, and if they're familiar with the power, they're going to know what sort of environmental factors to look for or rig up to facilitate detection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T22:36:13-07:00","id":911470,"title":"","content":"","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 06-10-2016, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T04:57:42-07:00","id":911578,"title":"","content":"Isn't lashing out done against one specific target (who can then lash back) ?<br /> <br /> And well, that seems to make sense, but I got a different vibe from the way the power was described. Basically, what I gatheredd was that no, you couldn't see an obfuscated character without auspex unless they attack you or someone who sees them points them out to you (an I think there was a roll there), BUT you can &quot;track&quot; them, meaning if you know something is going on (maybe unseen sense if it's not just for mortals), like if you know you're alone and you hear noise anyway, then, with a succesful roll, you can get a general idea where the vampire is. You don't see them, but you can guess they (and hopefuly not something else) are around and possibly steer clear from them or lay a physical trap and hope they'll step into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T06:36:00-07:00","id":911614,"title":"","content":"The fun thing about Disciplines in 2e is that they all build off the basic first (well, sometimes second) dot power in some way. So, in the case of Obfuscate, they all build off of Face in the Crowd or Touch of Shadow in some way, and ToS builds off of FitC. So, when looking at ways to notice an Obfuscated vampire, we just look at the first dot power.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If he\u2019s doing something that would draw attention, including but not limited to being violent, everyone around him must make a reflexive Wits + Composure roll to notice the commotion, penalized by the vampire\u2019s Obfuscate dots.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> This book quote tells you everything you need to know. If you have traps and the Obfuscate vampre sets one off, make a perception check. If the vampire is violent, perception check. If you need to worry about a hidden vampire, then you just need to arrange things so that he or she reveals themselves somehow. With Acute Senses, Bloodhound, Danger Sense and Trained Observer, its not hard to easily succeed at such a roll.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be aware and actively looking (that tends to be a Wits + Investigation roll), but you do need something around that the stealth-vamp can trigger to make you notice. You need the surrounding environment to aid you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T07:32:28-07:00","id":911642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911614#post911614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fun thing about Disciplines in 2e is that they all build off the basic first (well, sometimes second) dot power in some way. So, in the case of Obfuscate, they all build off of Face in the Crowd or Touch of Shadow in some way, and ToS builds off of FitC. So, when looking at ways to notice an Obfuscated vampire, we just look at the first dot power.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;If he\u2019s doing something that would draw attention, including but not limited to being violent, everyone around him must make a reflexive Wits + Composure roll to notice the commotion, penalized by the vampire\u2019s Obfuscate dots.&quot; </i><br /> <br /> This book quote tells you everything you need to know. If you have traps and the Obfuscate vampre sets one off, make a perception check. If the vampire is violent, perception check. If you need to worry about a hidden vampire, then you just need to arrange things so that he or she reveals themselves somehow. With Acute Senses, Bloodhound, Danger Sense and Trained Observer, its not hard to easily succeed at such a roll.<br /> <br /> You don't need to be aware and actively looking (that tends to be a Wits + Investigation roll), but you do need something around that the stealth-vamp can trigger to make you notice. You need the surrounding environment to aid you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a pretty good explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T09:09:42-07:00","id":911702,"title":"","content":"Note that the specific way Cloak of Night enhances Face in the Crowd is by removing some of its limitations.<br /> <br /> &quot;The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely. Rather than being overlooked or \u201cjust an average person,\u201d the vampire disappears from the perception of everyone around him.<br /> If the vampire attacks someone or cries out, Cloak of Night continues to obscure him, adding Obfuscate to the surprise roll. Only the struck victim can perceive the vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes on to say the vampire can still be tracked with indirect clues, but the vampire doesn't break the effect on himself by acting violently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:27:43-07:00","id":911847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911702#post911702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the specific way Cloak of Night enhances Face in the Crowd is by removing some of its limitations.<br /> <br /> &quot;The vampire can also spend a point of Vitae when activating Face in the Crowd to vanish completely. Rather than being overlooked or \u201cjust an average person,\u201d the vampire disappears from the perception of everyone around him.<br /> If the vampire attacks someone or cries out, Cloak of Night continues to obscure him, adding Obfuscate to the surprise roll. Only the struck victim can perceive the vampire.&quot;<br /> <br /> It goes on to say the vampire can still be tracked with indirect clues, but the vampire doesn't break the effect on himself by acting violently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Could you please list some examples on how this would work at the table? Both when someone could roll to see him and when they couldn't and etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T13:43:39-07:00","id":911856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911847#post911847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you please list some examples on how this would work at the table? Both when someone could roll to see him and when they couldn't and etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. So, what Cloak of Night essentially does is causes observers to ignore sensory information about the vampire. So if you look where he's standing, you don't see him. If he shouts, you don't hear him. But he's still actually there, and you can still observe the effects of his presence on the environment so if he opens a door, you see it open. If he steps on creaky floorboards, you hear them creak. If he bites some poor sap in the neck, you see her struggling against some invisible force.<br /> <br /> Anyone can attempt to track the vampire by these environmental signs of his presence - listening for footsteps, looking for where the rain seems to stop short of the ground, etc. This requires aWits + Resolve roll penalized by the vampire's Obfuscate, and often taken as an extended action. Success doesn't allow you to actually see him, just to know where he is. Another vampire who figures out where he is can initiate a Clash of Wills, and can see him if she wins the Clash. A human who figures out where he is just has a better idea of what direction to point her pepper spray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-10-2016, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:21:36-07:00","id":911882,"title":"","content":"Does Auspex give passive Obfuscate detection or do you have to initiate it? How about Kindred blood sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 06-10-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:27:03-07:00","id":911887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911882#post911882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Auspex give passive Obfuscate detection or do you have to initiate it? How about with Kindred blood sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Auspex can initiate a Clash of Wills with an Obfuscated vampire, but it does have to be activated. Kindred senses add a bonus to the roll to track an Obfuscated vampire by environmental signs of their presence. And Auspex also adds to effective Blood Potency for the purposes of Kindred senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T14:49:13-07:00","id":911910,"title":"","content":"That's mostly what I gathered, so good to know. I'm intrigued by the last part about the clash of wills. Are we talking about a vampire who knows auspex ? Because I would be normally make a passive roll for that as long as the two vampires are in the same room. The auspex vampire wouldn't automatically know there is another one around (lthough the player probably would), but it would be a classic case of detection vs stealth roll.<br /> <br /> Of course, the thing is there's pretty much no other way for anyone but a vampire with auspex o see through the thing. Do werewolves have similar powers with 2nd Ed gifts ? Wonder if a clash of wills without the needed discipline would work in specific conditions, like if a vampire has been successful in tracking an obfuscated one and has a clear lign of view and a good idea where they are. In the obfuscate vs not-auspex case, it would be BP+obf vs BP. Pretty stacked in favor of the obfuscated vampire, at least until we start considering vastly different BPs. Even then, since this specific power is level 3, a BP1 vampire would only start being equalized by a BP4 one. Looking for a decent houserule that gives the auspex-less vampire a shot, even a slim one. Go for the old 10 again doesn't work and 1s remove a success ? Impose a penalty equal to the discipline you want to counter (hat might be a bit much) ? I'm liking the first idea :<br /> <br /> So without auspex, to see an obfuscated vampire, you need to successfully track them, and then succeed at a clash of will where you only roll your BP, don't reroll 10s and lose a success if you roll a 1.<br /> <br /> I'm splitting hair here, and I doubt I'll ever need that houserule, but I'll keep that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:38:24-07:00","id":911963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911856#post911856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. So, what Cloak of Night essentially does is causes observers to ignore sensory information about the vampire. So if you look where he's standing, you don't see him. If he shouts, you don't hear him. But he's still actually there, and you can still observe the effects of his presence on the environment so if he opens a door, you see it open. If he steps on creaky floorboards, you hear them creak. If he bites some poor sap in the neck, you see her struggling against some invisible force.<br /> <br /> Anyone can attempt to track the vampire by these environmental signs of his presence - listening for footsteps, looking for where the rain seems to stop short of the ground, etc. This requires aWits + Resolve roll penalized by the vampire's Obfuscate, and often taken as an extended action. Success doesn't allow you to actually see him, just to know where he is. Another vampire who figures out where he is can initiate a Clash of Wills, and can see him if she wins the Clash. A human who figures out where he is just has a better idea of what direction to point her pepper spray.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Does the attacked character see the vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:39:28-07:00","id":911964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911963#post911963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the attacked character see the vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sorry I forgot to mention that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:45:05-07:00","id":911971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911964#post911964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, sorry I forgot to mention that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unrelated to the original but related to this. <br /> <br /> By mixing Celerity and Obfuscate could the following devotions be made<br /> <br /> Strike from the Shadows<br /> <br /> Ob 3 Celerity 3<br /> <br /> You can spend a point of viate after making a susscful attack to disappear again before the attacked character sees you<br /> <br /> Ob 3 Celerity 1<br /> <br /> Add you Ob to your defense in addation to your Celerity as you begin to disappear around the edges and almost flicker in and out. (Got the Idea from the Changeling hack that adds their Wyrds to defense )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T17:32:33-07:00","id":911992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911971#post911971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated to the original but related to this. <br /> <br /> By mixing Celerity and Obfuscate could the following devotions be made<br /> <br /> Strike from the Shadows<br /> <br /> Ob 3 Celerity 3<br /> <br /> You can spend a point of viate after making a susscful attack to disappear again before the attacked character sees you</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I would probably charge 2 Vitae instead of 1 for an effect like that, and allow the target to make a reflexive contested roll or something to give them a chance to notice you. I'd also probably limit it to (Celerity) uses per Scene and only require Celerity 1 for the Devotion. But the core idea seems fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911971#post911971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ob 3 Celerity 1<br /> <br /> Add you Ob to your defense in addation to your Celerity as you begin to disappear around the edges and almost flicker in and out. (Got the Idea from the Changeling hack that adds their Wyrds to defense )</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I'm not feeling this one. Celerity already allows you to do the anime &quot;move so fast you disappear&quot; thing, so I don't see how using Obfuscate to actually disappear would really enhance that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:34:44-07:00","id":912077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911992#post911992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmm... I'm not feeling this one. Celerity already allows you to do the anime &amp;quot;move so fast you disappear&amp;quot; thing, so I don't see how using Obfuscate to actually disappear would really enhance that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Originally I thought of it as a devotion being solely Ob. The idea was you're manipulation of their perception makes it harder for them to hit you. You always seem a little more to the left or right or close or further away then you really are. I figured if Ob 1 could make eyes slide off you it was within the realm of Ob to make room to manipulate that for more combative use","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T22:45:51-07:00","id":912110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=912077#post912077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Originally I thought of it as a devotion being solely Ob. The idea was you're manipulation of their perception makes it harder for them to hit you. You always seem a little more to the left or right or close or further away then you really are. I figured if Ob 1 could make eyes slide off you it was within the realm of Ob to make room to manipulate that for more combative use</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok, I see what you're going for. How about instead of a Devotion, you make a Fighting Style with Obfuscate as a Prerequisite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T04:07:07-07:00","id":912186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911856#post911856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. So, what Cloak of Night essentially does is causes observers to ignore sensory information about the vampire. So if you look where he's standing, you don't see him. If he shouts, you don't hear him. But he's still actually there, and you can still observe the effects of his presence on the environment so if he opens a door, you see it open. If he steps on creaky floorboards, you hear them creak. If he bites some poor sap in the neck, you see her struggling against some invisible force.<br /> <br /> Anyone can attempt to track the vampire by these environmental signs of his presence - listening for footsteps, looking for where the rain seems to stop short of the ground, etc. This requires aWits + Resolve roll penalized by the vampire's Obfuscate, and often taken as an extended action. Success doesn't allow you to actually see him, just to know where he is. Another vampire who figures out where he is can initiate a Clash of Wills, and can see him if she wins the Clash. A human who figures out where he is just has a better idea of what direction to point her pepper spray.</div> </div> </div> </div> On a note, I personally read the situation where, if you see an invisible vampire struggling with someone grappling, that pretty much is an obvious &quot;tracked down&quot; success. At this point, I call for the original Perception check to break Obfuscate, as per first dot power.<br /> <br /> The reason for this is that, if you want to grab someone and feed from them obviously like this? Then that's what using the Touch of Shadow power on other living persons is for. You make people ignore the struggle as a whole. You don't get to be invisible when everyone has an obvious lock on your position and knows where to look to see you. I don't think that staying invisible when you're being so obvious is thematically appropriate for the power. I really don't think that's how the power is meant to work.<br /> <br /> In short, while the third dot power modifies the first dot, I don't believe that it eliminates the Perception check entirely. It just narrows the situations in which you apply that Perception check to after the tracking roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-11-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T05:55:13-07:00","id":912202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=912110#post912110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, ok, I see what you're going for. How about instead of a Devotion, you make a Fighting Style with Obfuscate as a Prerequisite?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very cool idea. I wouldn't even know where to begin for a discipline based fighting style. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> Level 1 minus obfuscate from perception check to resist surprise attack<br /> <br /> Level 2 add Obfuscate to defense when Ob 1 or 2 is active, clashing with Auspex, if lose, lose the defense bonus <br /> <br /> Level 3 ??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:08:10-07:00","id":912205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=911992#post911992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. I would probably charge 2 Vitae instead of 1 for an effect like that, and allow the target to make a reflexive contested roll or something to give them a chance to notice you. I'd also probably limit it to (Celerity) uses per Scene and only require Celerity 1 for the Devotion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could that roll be a simple wits+composure test with a target successes equal to the celerity level of the attacker? Or is more appropriate a contested on wits+composure vs. Wits+stealth/athlethics maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T07:37:41-07:00","id":912228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=912202#post912202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very cool idea. I wouldn't even know where to begin for a discipline based fighting style. Suggestions?<br /> <br /> Level 1 minus obfuscate from perception check to resist surprise attack<br /> <br /> Level 2 add Obfuscate to defense when Ob 1 or 2 is active, clashing with Auspex, if lose, lose the defense bonus <br /> <br /> Level 3 ??</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... Obfuscate 3 already adds you Ob dots to your surprise rolls, so the first dot seems a little redundant. The second one doesn't work because you can't have Obfuscate active in combat (attacking someone is one of the rings that breaks Obfuscate), but the idea behind it is good. <br /> <br /> How about if the first dot makes opponents subconsciously consider you a low-priority target in combat? Maybe it reduces your own Initiative by your Obfuscate dots, but opponents with higher Initiative than you can't attack you on the first turn of combat, or something like that. Then the second dot could just add your Obfuscate dots to Dodge rolls, which gets your idea of being harder to hit, without adding a lot of extra Contested actions, plus it keeps the Fighting Style highly defensive, which is more on-theme for Obfuscate. Then you want the third dot to be the iconic ability of the style, something that lets you appear and disappear mid-combat. Maybe piggyback it off the second dot, letting you activate Obfuscate 3 reflexively after a dodge that reduces the attacker's successes to 0?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=912205#post912205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could that roll be a simple wits+composure test with a target successes equal to the celerity level of the attacker? Or is more appropriate a contested on wits+composure vs. Wits+stealth/athlethics maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say either contested Wits + Composure vs. Wits + Stealth, or maybe Wits + Composure - Obfuscate. Target successes isn't usually a thing outside of extended actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-11-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T09:07:36-07:00","id":912271,"title":"","content":"For the two questions that were about lashing out. ( quoting on my phone is really hard &gt;.&lt; ) <br /> <br /> I would think you need to be aware they are there. Perceptions, investigations, or you just know for whatever reason. <br /> <br /> And yes, if you are lashed out on, you can either fight it or flee/back down/submit. <br /> <br /> It is specifically mentioned that lashing can shatter obfuscate, which is why I mentioned it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T20:21:52-07:00","id":912603,"title":"","content":"Assuming you mean fully invisble as per Cloak of Night:<br /> Lashing out can shatter Obfuscate but only if you can already see the Obfuscated vampire as you need to be able to sense their beast.<br /> All the usual &quot;tracking invisible person&quot; methods work like setting off sprinkler systems or covering the ground with flour/sawdust/etc.<br /> If you don't have Auspex or access to any other indirect tracking methods your best bet is to goad the vampire into frenzy so that they attack you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T20:42:32-07:00","id":913196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=912603#post912603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you mean fully invisble as per Cloak of Night:<br /> Lashing out can shatter Obfuscate but only if you can already see the Obfuscated vampire as you need to be able to sense their beast.<br /> All the usual &quot;tracking invisible person&quot; methods work like setting off sprinkler systems or covering the ground with flour/sawdust/etc.<br /> If you don't have Auspex or access to any other indirect tracking methods your best bet is to goad the vampire into frenzy so that they attack you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the kindred does have to see the kindred to lash right? Like someone with Auspex or someone he is fighting could lash. but you can't lash knowing the kindred is in the room but not where right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T22:58:09-07:00","id":913251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/911346-obfuscate-question?p=913196#post913196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But the kindred does have to see the kindred to lash right? Like someone with Auspex or someone he is fighting could lash. but you can't lash knowing the kindred is in the room but not where right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. To lash out the kindred must SEE the obfuscate kindred winning the clash of will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}